<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 120,000 tonnes wheat, 60,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 120,000 tonnes wheat, 60,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 60,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 20,000 of Canadian wheat, 40,000 of Australian wheat, 20,000 of U.S. barley and 40,000 of Australian barley at its weekly tender.</p>
<p>These are for March shipment.</p>
<p>The tender results details are as follows, in tonnes.</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 60,000	   Dark northern spring   40,000</p>
<p>				   Hard red winter</p>
<p>				    (13 percent protein)  20,000</p>
<p> Canada     20,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>								  20,000</p>
<p> Australia  40,000	   Standard white	   40,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 20,000	   Feed			 20,000</p>
<p> Australia  40,000	   Feed			 20,000</p>
<p>				   Food			 20,000</p>
</text>
